Spidy Editor
============

Spidy Editor is a renamed, Windows-hardened edition of ghost-editor by kurbaitaev
(https://github.com/kurbaitaev/ghost-editor), used and redistributed under the MIT
licence. The original copyright notice is reproduced in LICENSE and applies to the
whole work:

    Copyright (c) 2026 kurbaitaev

Original work
-------------
The editor, its steps and scripts, the recipes/ styles, templates, styles library,
documentation and the creative direction come from ghost-editor.

Changes in this edition
-----------------------
- Windows port: the pipeline runs natively (no Git Bash, no WSL). Every step that was
  a shell script now has a Python implementation; the .sh files remain thin wrappers
  for macOS and Linux.
- Launcher: `spidy` / `spidy.cmd` find a real Python (skipping the Microsoft Store
  alias) and refresh PATH from the registry, so node, npx and ffmpeg are visible in
  sessions that started before those tools were installed.
- Rendering: HyperFrames is invoked through node's npx entry point (cmd.exe splits
  arguments containing spaces), and renders use the browser and ffmpeg already on the
  machine instead of downloading a managed Chrome.
- Encoding: UTF-8 is forced for every text read/write and for child processes.
- Rebranding: the skill is published as Spidy Editor (skill ID `spidy-editor`), with
  `ghost` kept as an alias; README, INSTALL and WINDOWS docs rewritten for the new
  name and for Windows-first installation.
- Personal demo media from the original project (recorded footage, style grids) is
  not redistributed here. The media library (SFX, music, emoji, LUTs, models) is
  downloaded at install time; manifests ship in this repository.

